% ============================================================================
% radius-definition.query.adj — a worked recall over the geometry
% radius-definition library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does radius mean
% for a sphere?": it states no geometry fact of its own — it only `import`s
% the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `radius_definition` rows and returns the defining phrase + the
% table's source/locator/trust. A shape the cited sentence does not name
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents a definition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli radius-definition.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "radius-definition.adj"

? radius_definition(sphere, $D)                       % expect center_to_surface
? radius_definition($Shape, center_to_perimeter)      % reverse bind — expect circle
? radius_definition(cube, $D)                         % expect abstain — the cited sentence names only circle and sphere
